WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.634
I'm Juan Cisco. Marnie.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.136
Hi. I'm running. Running for U.S.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.538
Congress, running in Arizona's

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.773
Sixth District,

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.308
a key race and the battle

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.110
for control of the U.S. House.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.144
I can answer any questions for you

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:11.878
before you vote.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:12.645
Juan Cisco.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.614
Manny was born in Mexico,

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.582
immigrated here

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.950
to Tucson, Arizona,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.718
with his family at age 11.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.652
Nice to meet you.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.688
He's also a Republican.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.189
I'm someone that grew up here

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.991
in a very Democrat area

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.493
in the state of Arizona.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.228
As a first generation

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.430
Hispanic Republican, so that really

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.333
puts me in a different light,

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.167
I think, of saying, well,

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.402
how do you see the issues?

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.736
I see them very uniquely

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.071
as a conservative,

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.073
especially on economy issues

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.175
he believes are driving voters this year,

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.209
all voters.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.277
When people ask me, hey,

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.412
what are the Hispanic issues

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.880
we should be focusing on?

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.848
I kind of chuckle a little bit

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:49.549
and I say, well,

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.284
there are no Hispanic issues.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.420
There are issues that impact everyone.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.088
I'm paying the same thing for guys

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:55.789
milk and eggs

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.058
that the person next door is paying,

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.292
that they're not Hispanic.

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.960
Thank you all for being here.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.094
Good.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.362
I just bought a companion

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.430
to make that point.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.164
He invited

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.365
local small business

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.933
owners to his campaign office

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.435
to discuss their challenges.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.437
No traffic it's affected us a lot.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.371
The economy.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.272
Like when I'm young,

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:15.308
there are only 13 Hispanic Republicans

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:16.810
now serving in the House.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.845
Cisco Marney is one of 33

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.014
Hispanic GOP candidates on the ballot

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:21.781
this year.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.483
Part of a concerted leadership

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.350
effort to boost

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.652
their ranks in the chamber.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.053
Do you feel comfortable

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:29.489
with the way that leaders in your party

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.391
have expressed themselves

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.526
vis-a-vis the Hispanic community?

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:34.561
Well, I can only control

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.862
how I express myself

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.230
with the Hispanic community.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:37.664
And I

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:38.765
and I'm very proud of the way

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.666
that we've done it.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.266
They argue

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.569
Democrats are taking Hispanic voters

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.603
for granted.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.305
I think the Republican Party

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.639
is recognizing

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.676
that it's right there for the taking

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.377
if the right message is there

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:52.912
and the right messenger as well.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.913
And that's where candidates like

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:54.781
myself come in.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:58.418
Helder Toasty is doing just that.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.319
I'm here with Bob Moss,

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.420
which is an effort to get Latinos

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.421
to actually go vote,

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.323
running a new program for Senate

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.291
Republicans called Vamos.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.060
We walked with him through neighborhoods

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:07.861
in Nevada

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:09.229
as he searched for votes

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:09.863
in growing

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.264
Hispanic communities

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.566
just a few miles from the Vegas Strip.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:14.267
This,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.035
as far as I know,

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.538
has historically been pretty blue Yeah.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.206
I mean, traditionally, Democrats

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.008
have gotten 80. 90% of the vote here.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:22.909
So the reason we're here

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.310
is to get votes

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.112
where we traditionally haven't shown up.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.847
He uses a special app,

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.849
micro-targeting potential voters.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.617
We've loaded

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:31.918
in all of the different names

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:32.418
of the voters

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.586
that we're trying to talk to.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.220
This particular

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.555
voters, a weak Republican,

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:36.890
which means they're on the team.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.457
They don't always

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.858
show up in the general election.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:39.526
Hi there.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:40.727
This GOP ground

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.061
operation is in nine

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.863
states with critical Senate races

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.597
this year.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.532
The whole point of the program

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.634
is to just talk to Hispanic voters

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.768
because when you're in a get out

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.403
the vote phase,

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.171
these voters are the ones

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.138
who get left behind.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:52.906
Not like this.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:53.706
I haven't decided

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.008
which party I'll go with.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.210
Maria, Mel Goza is exactly

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.111
the kind of voter

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:00.413
Republicans are trying to attract by them

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.147
from a deal.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.582
I didn't promise many things,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.150
but I feel like he hasn't delivered

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:06.986
the yellow to Partido

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:07.921
and the other party.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:08.922
I don't know much about it.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:11.624
Knows not not so much there, she said.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:12.425
Until now,

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.761
neither Republicans nor Democrats

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.396
